vices","fingerprint":"9feeddab124dd90d4b0c2fddeda5d9af655f0404b17d3dbf8b991e0508c480ce","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"General GNS 113 enrichment: Reference Sources and Services","sourceKind":"general_gns113","reviewedFromLocalFile":false},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_gns113_200_v1","sourceReference":"General GNS 113 enrichment: Reference Sources and Services","contentAndAnswerCheckCompleted":true,"humanVerificationRequired":true},"options":[{"id":"bd36dea1-155c-5cfc-9801-6661ac23a413","text":"An anonymous social-media comment","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"5a8ba500-c10c-5c75-963c-91b62542dad1","text":"A random advertisement","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"994af768-85b4-5b5d-b834-063534d7ff24","text":"A circulation notice","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"7dcc5248-14ae-5c70-af5c-05315c7a796a","text":"A reputable subject encyclopedia","isCorrect":true,"position":3}]},{"id":"0b2ab073-abfc-50a7-9fda-6671cb301185","position":118,"prompt":"Two online reference sources disagree on a statistic. What is the best response?","explanation":"Source evaluation and verification are necessary when reference information conflicts.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"hard","cognitive":"analysis","topic":"Reference Sources and Services","fingerprint":"29733551b029e5e52e16404bfd707d949bd16cd1203cbb34dd72900946d2e0fc","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"General GNS 113 enrichment: Reference Sources and Services","sourceKind":"general_gns113","reviewedFromLocalFile":false},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_gns113_200_v1","sourceReference":"General GNS 113 enrichment: Reference Sources and Services","contentAndAnswerCheckCompleted":true,"humanVerificationRequired":true},"options":[{"id":"b38b991f-0dfb-5246-aea3-8b14c0eb9973","text":"Average them without investigation","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"8a156797-2ef1-5b2c-8149-cd3a2afdb85f","text":"Cite both as equally current","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"1120a620-645c-5eb5-97a6-37a402f0f8ac","text":"